{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1772901200,"nonce":"kEnXyrGgC4OjYYXtXgeNRx1X8b4=","title":"auth-merge: auto-build dist after merge when src/ changed","message":"auth-merge.sh has restart_mandible_if_dist_changed() which detects dist changes and restarts the daemon, but has no build step. The expected workflow requires agents to build and commit dist in the feature branch before submitting the auth request. When agents forget (or follow the CLAUDE.md \"do not commit dist in feature branches\" instruction literally), the dist is not updated and the daemon stays on old code.\n\nFix: after a successful git merge, if src/ or ui/src/ changed, run npm run build in the repo root, stage the output with git add -u dist/ ui/dist/, and commit it using the agent signing key. Then restart_mandible_if_dist_changed will detect the new dist and trigger the daemon restart as normal.","files":null}]}